source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-24
observed: With every `}}` hidden behind a backslash pair the run holds no closer at all, so Jira shows the first pair literally and breaks on the second, the last run of its token; jiro refuses the span too and reads the same two backslashes and hard break.
-- input.jira --
{{a\\}}b\\}}
-- rendered.html --
<p>{{a\\}}b<br class="atl-forced-newline" />}}</p>
-- want.md --
{{a\\\\}}b\
}}
-- warnings.json --
[]
